 Sheet merged in) · <b>S05</b> Room phrasing classes: 'bed', 'Room', 'Rm. #', bare number, no room, a name only; the picker opened on a room box</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U3</b> A box that starts with a room number (e.g. 'bed 415…') shows a room chip, and the picker suggests that room's patient. The physician still taps to assign; nothing auto-assigns. (UAT TC-04; TFA-92582 AC 4; TFA-92582 step 4; TFA-92583 AC 3)</li><li><b>U6</b> No auto-assignment anywhere: the app never splits one dictation across patients, never routes by name or room, and never merges boxes. There is no AI routing. (UAT TC-04; TFA-92582 AC 2; TFA-92583 AC 2)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Equivalence classes (equivalence) — Check the same rule again with another class of input (Hospital / Nursing Home, other data); every class has to be right.</p><p><b>Given </b>QA Hosp Patel in room 415, QA Hosp Ortiz in room 416</p><p><b>When </b>Type into one box, replacing the text each time: 'bed 415 seen at 7, comfortable.' (then open Assign to patient on it and close the picker), 'Room 415: pain 3/10, on oral analgesia.', 'Rm. #415 — dressing changed.', '415 — afebrile, eating breakfast.', 'Looks better this morning, lungs clear.', 'QA Hosp Ortiz looks be …</p><p><b>Then </b>Each of the four room forms shows the chip and suggests Patel; the picker opened on the room box lists Patel (where he sits is recorded for Q1); the no-room text and the name-only text show no chip and no suggestion, and the name never routes the box to Ortiz; no text reaches either chart without a tap</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>oracle.mjs: cp1 and cp3–cp5 mustContain 'Rm 415' and '415 · QA Hosp Patel', mustNotContain 'Re-assign' (U3). cp2 (picker open on the room box) mustContain 'Assign to patient', 'Search room or name', '415 · QA Hosp Patel', mustNotContain 'Re-assign'; Patel's place in the list and any mark are recorded for Q1. cp6 mustNotContain 'Rm 415' and 'Matches on your list'. …</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>dev unit U14; test method AGENT · Browser agent; lane planned in the matrix: browser agent (blocked)</p><p><small>S05 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-04.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>e02167f</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-12T18:24:27Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>.</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AGENT · Browser agent — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>dev</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-04 Quick Dictation (Hospital only; TC-05 Rounding Sheet merged in) · <b>Section:</b> A1 · Home Screen &amp; Dashboard · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-04/S05</p><p><b>Room phrasing classes: 'bed', 'Room', 'Rm. #', bare number, no room, a name only; the picker opened on a room box</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92582 Quick Dictation (ready for qa); TFA-92583 Rounding Sheet (ready for qa)</p><p><b>Result:</b> Pass from <code>scripts/oracle.mjs</code> on the saved evidence (<code>generated/tc04s05/verdict.json</code>). Agent: 43 turns, 124 s, $0.23.</p><p><b>Recorded (evidence only):</b></p><ul><li>s05-picker-room.md: (Q1: where Patel sits in the picker opened on his room's box) pass: in order: &quot;415 · QA TC-04-S05 QA Hosp Patel LS0A&quot; &lt; &quot;416 · QA TC-04-S05 QA Hosp Ortiz LS0A&quot; (in from &quot;Search room or name&quot;)</li></ul><p><b>Plan:</b> unit U14 (#14, ready-for-qa, ui-only) — Quick Dictation: room phrasing classes. Quick Dictation compartments belong to the account; quickDictation:list counts.</p><p><b>Checked by Quinn's runner</b> (<code>ledger.md</code> #14, U14; checked: yes): <b>Pass</b> — room chip + 'Matches on your list' suggestion for Bed/Room/Rm/bare numbers, none without a room, name match; nothing auto-assigns; assign appends verbatim</p>","environment":"default","setup":[],"